  "body": {
    "id": "lem:finite-honest-confidence",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "For every finite revealed graph \\(G\\), every \\(0<\\alpha<1\\), and every \\(y\\in\\mathcal M_n(G)\\), the selected certified procedure satisfies\n\\[\n\\Pr_{\\mathcal D_G}\\!\\left\\{\\tau_n\\in\\mathcal C_\\alpha(G,Z,Y^{\\mathrm{obs}})\\mid G\\right\\}\\ge1-\\alpha.\n\\]",
    "free_symbols": [
      "G",
      "\\alpha",
      "y",
      "\\mathcal M_n(G)",
      "\\mathcal D_G",
      "\\tau_n",
      "\\mathcal C_\\alpha(G,Z,Y^{\\mathrm{obs}})",
      "Z",
      "Y^{\\mathrm{obs}}"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:outcome-class",
      "def:certified-procedure",
      "def:confidence-set",
      "lem:schur-certificate"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Fix a finite revealed graph \\(G\\), a schedule\n\\(y\\in\\mathcal M_n(G)\\), and \\(\\alpha\\in(0,1)\\).  If the certified\nprocedure selects the seed branch, Lemma~\\(\\mathrm{lem{:}schur\\mbox{-}certificate}\\)\ngives\n\\[\n\\mathbb E_{\\mathcal D_G,y}\n\\left[(\\widehat\\tau_{\\mathrm{cert}}-\\tau_n)^2\\mid G\\right]\n\\le U(G,k_n)=\\overline U(G).\n\\tag{21}\n\\]\nOn either fallback branch, the report is \\(\\mu_1\\), so its error for\n\\(\\tau_n=\\mu_1-\\mu_0\\) equals \\(\\mu_0\\).  By Cauchy--Schwarz and the\ncontrol endpoint restriction,\n\\[\n(\\widehat\\tau_{\\mathrm{cert}}-\\tau_n)^2\n=\\mu_0^2\n\\le\\frac1n\\sum_i b_i^2\n\\le1=\\overline U(G).\n\\tag{22}\n\\]\nThus (21) holds for the selected procedure on every branch.  Moreover,\n\\(\\overline U(G)>0\\): it equals one on a fallback branch, while on the seed\nbranch \\(U(G,k_n)\\ge2/k_n>0\\).  Since also \\(\\alpha>0\\), Markov's\ninequality applied conditionally on \\(G\\) to the nonnegative squared error\nin (21) yields\n\\[\n\\Pr_{\\mathcal D_G}\\!\\left\\{\n|\\widehat\\tau_{\\mathrm{cert}}-\\tau_n|\n>\\sqrt{\\overline U(G)/\\alpha}\n\\,\\middle|\\,G\\right\\}\n\\le\\alpha.\n\\tag{23}\n\\]\n\nThe two endpoint restrictions and Cauchy--Schwarz also give\n\\[\n|\\mu_1|\\le\n\\left(\\frac1n\\sum_i a_i^2\\right)^{1/2}\\le1,\n\\qquad\n|\\mu_0|\\le\n\\left(\\frac1n\\sum_i b_i^2\\right)^{1/2}\\le1.\n\\tag{24}\n\\]\nHence \\(\\tau_n=\\mu_1-\\mu_0\\in[-2,2]\\).  On the complement of the event\nin (23), \\(\\tau_n\\) lies in the untruncated interval centered at\n\\(\\widehat\\tau_{\\mathrm{cert}}\\) with radius\n\\(\\sqrt{\\overline U(G)/\\alpha}\\), and (24) places it in \\([-2,2]\\).\nIt therefore lies in their intersection\n\\(\\mathcal C_\\alpha(G,Z,Y^{\\mathrm{obs}})\\).  Taking probabilities and\nusing (23) proves\n\\[\n\\Pr_{\\mathcal D_G}\\!\\left\\{\n\\tau_n\\in\\mathcal C_\\alpha(G,Z,Y^{\\mathrm{obs}})\\mid G\n\\right\\}\\ge1-\\alpha.\n\\]",
